#### Barrel Electromagnetic Calorimeter

The Barrel Electromagnetic Calorimeter [53] (BEMC) is a scintillator-lead sampling calorimeter located outside the TPC3 and within the STAR magnet coils, as can be seen from figure 2.2. Its active volume has a pseudo-rapidity coverage equal to \(-1<\eta<1\) and it extends \(2\pi\) in azimuth. The inner radius of the BEMC, determined at the front plate, is equal to 223.5 cm, its outer

