The PMTs of the BEMC are of the type _Electron Tube Inc. model 9125B_ and were required to have a quantum efficiency of at least 10% at \(\lambda=420\,\mathrm{nm}\) upon installation. The mean efficiency was found to be 13.3%. Only PMTs which had a non-linearity less than 2% at a peak current of 20 mA were installed. The high voltage on the 11 dynodes is regulated by a Cockroft-Walton type base which provides a voltage division ratio of \(\{2:1:1:1:1:1:2:3:4:3\}\). The high voltage on these bases can be remotely steered through a serial slow controls network. Further details on the BEMC optical structure, its mechanical design, as well as performance estimates can be found in [11].

